ics","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift","permalink":"an-object-is-placed-at-a-distance-of-12-cm-from-a-convex-len-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-lmpa1havcrea5hbg","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"An object is placed at a distance of 12 cm from a convex lens. A convex mirror of focal length 15 cm is placed on other side of lens at 8 cm as shown in the figure. Image of object coincides with the object.<br><br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 167 English\"></picture><br>When the convex mirror is removed, a real and inverted image is formed at a position. The distance of the image from the object will be .............. (cm)","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"50","explanation":"<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzhh0r/a634d71a-2870-451a-a5a8-fad0bd25d866/8cb7c3b0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzhh0s-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzhh0r/a634d71a-2870-451a-a5a8-fad0bd25d866/8cb7c3b0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzhh0s-500w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzhh0r/a634d71a-2870-451a-a5a8-fad0bd25d866/8cb7c3b0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzhh0s-680w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 860px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzhh0r/a634d71a-2870-451a-a5a8-fad0bd25d866/8cb7c3b0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzhh0s-860w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzhh0r/a634d71a-2870-451a-a5a8-fad0bd25d866/8cb7c3b0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzhh0s.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 167 English Explanation\"></picture> <br><br>For the object to coincide with image, the light must fall perpendicularly to mirror. Which means that the light will have to converge at C of mirror. Without the mirror also, the light would coverage at C.<br><br>So the distance is : 12 + 8 + 30 = 50 cm"},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"एक वस्तु को उत्तल लेंस से 12 सेमी की दूरी पर रखा गया है। एक उत्तल दर्पण जिसकी फोकल लंबाई 15 सेमी है, लेंस की अन्य ओर 8 सेमी पर रखा गया है जैसा कि चित्र में दिखाया गया है। वस्तु का प्रतिबिंब वस्तु के साथ मेल खाता है।<br><br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten14c8/0ba4420e-14e0-441d-a068-4e543044c799/2487a290-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten14c9.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 167 Hindi\"></picture><br>जब उत्तल दर्पण को हटा दिया जाता है, एक वास्तविक और उलटा प्रतिबिंब एक स्थिति में बनता है। वस्तु से प्रतिबिंब की दूरी .............. (सेमी) होगी","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"50","explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"lenses","type":"integer","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-evening-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-evening-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1ktbvwych","chapter":"laws-of-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift","permalink":"the-coefficient-of-static-friction-between-two-blocks-is-05-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-7bhwf4qmervepg4w","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"The coefficient of static friction between two blocks is 0.5 and the table is smooth. The maximum horizontal force that can be applied to move the blocks together is .................. N. (take g = 10 ms<sup>-2</sup>)<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kten36yn/d691372d-c3a1-48f3-8679-ac93454d2db1/5e2c68f0-125d-11ec-a4fb-5347f21481c0/file-1kten36yo.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 92 English\">","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"15","explanation":"F = 3a (For system) ............ (i)<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktkzk5pq/e3ba47ac-372e-4b8e-aefb-5cc7f46fdfa4/d76977f0-15da-11ec-9f9f-77d6d4b83b50/file-1ktkzk5pr.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Evening Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 92 English Explanation\"> <br><br>fs<sub>max</sub> = 1a (for 1 kg block) ............ (ii)<br><br><mjx-c